  "usage": {
    "summary": "`good-number-input` is a numeric field with a minus button on the left and a plus button on the right. It starts at `0`, moves in steps of `1`, and has a minimum of `0` and no maximum unless configured. Set `min`, `max`, and `step` to finite numbers; a nonpositive or nonfinite step falls back to `1`. If `max` is below `min`, the effective maximum equals the minimum.",
